BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23231Z
UID:MZ1B23t3Mw-8221312781@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260519T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260519T143000
SUMMARY:Journalist safety in the US: Crowds, protests, and events
URL:http://cpj.org/USJANcrowds
DESCRIPTION:Local and international journalists are gearing up to cover multiple major events in the U.S. this year -- including the World Cup and midterm elections -- and may face heightened risks as a result. Join the U.S. Journalist Assistance Network for a free roundtable focused on best practices for interacting with police and federal law enforcement\, crossing borders amid increased screenings\, preparing for device searches or seizures\, knowing your rights in the context of arrest or detention\, and navigating crowd or police violence at matches and rallies. The roundtable will feature legal and safety experts from Freedom of the Press Foundation\, International Women’s Media Foundation\, Kuck Baxter LLC\, and Reporters Committee for Freedom of the Press??'and will be moderated by PEN America. 
LOCATION:
END:VEVENT





BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23232Z
UID:vjLeX04c0M-8221920327@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T200000
SUMMARY:An Inside Look at Creator Journalism
URL:http://www.eventbrite.com/e/an-inside-look-at-creator-journalism-tickets-1988732588708?aff=oddtdtcreator
DESCRIPTION:Join SPJ Georgia for a virtual nuts and bolts discussion about the world of independent\, audience-driven publishing -- what it is\, how to get started and how to keep it going and growing.

Panelists:
Michele Hornish\, communications professional and author of the Substack newsletter 'Small Deeds Done'
Martin Kuz\, independent journalist and author of the Substack newsletter 'Reporting on Ukraine'
Liz Kelly Nelson\, co-founder of Project C\, a home for journalists navigating the independent journalism creator economy

Moderator: Patty Rasmussen\, independent journalist and SPJ GA Freelance Chair

The workshop is free for SPJ members. $10 for non-members. 
LOCATION:
END:VEVENT





